    "evidence_summary": "OWASP Agent Memory Guard protects AI agents from memory poisoning, persistent memory corruption, data exfiltration and malicious behavior across sessions.；Unit 42 demonstrates a proof of concept where indirect prompt injection silently poisons long-term agent memory and persists malicious instructions across sessions.；OWASP recommends validating and sanitizing data before storing agent memory, isolating memory, setting expiration and size limits, auditing sensitive data, and using cryptographic integrity checks.；LangChain documents short-term and long-term memory concepts, including LangGraph long-term memories stored as JSON documents under namespaces and keys.；Defines MemoryItem v0.1, memory types, lifecycle, source, write_policy, security, retrieval and integrity fields.",
